<title>USA: Penederm says FDA oks use of Avita for acne.</title>
<headline>Penederm says FDA oks use of Avita for acne.</headline>
<dateline>FOSTER CITY, Calif. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Penederm Inc said Thursday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has approved Penederm's AVITA cream for treating acne.</p>
<p>AVITA in gel form was granted contingent approval, pending expiration of a patent held by Johnson &amp; Johnson in January 1998.</p>
<p>The company said AVITA is its second prescription product to receive FDA approval in the last four months.</p>
</text>
